      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that makes sense. so if the lecithin headgroups are repelling each other and causing that depletion, does that mean the droplets are more likely to coalesce? i'm seeing some pretty significant droplet growth right before the separation happens. is there a way to use a different emulsifier or modify the lecithin concentration to stop that kinetic instability from taking over?",
